ithub.com/yizhangzzz/imagenet","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Lua","description":null,"topics":[],"score":214076,"global_rank":253809},{"name":"jvtrigueros/hugsql-lightning","owner":"jvtrigueros","html_url":"https://github.com/jvtrigueros/hugsql-lightning","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Clojure","description":"Ligthning Talk for Seajure Nov 2019","topics":[],"score":214076,"global_rank":253811},{"name":"Chrysippean/MNIST-Handwriting-Recognition","owner":"Chrysippean","html_url":"https://github.com/Chrysippean/MNIST-Handwriting-Recognition","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"MATLAB","description":"We use neural networks in order to construct an algorithm that identifies MNIST Handwriting digits from 0-9. We will start from a simple one-layer network, then on to a two-layer network, and we will generalize the logistics of our algorithm into neural networks with more layers.","topics":[],"score":214073,"global_rank":253814},{"name":"Chrysippean/Music-Clustering-and-Classification","owner":"Chrysippean","html_url":"https://github.com/Chrysippean/Music-Clustering-and-Classification","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"MATLAB","description":"Given a database of music, we apply three supervised learning techniques in order make correct distinctions between separate genres of music. We will then use the information gathered from the learning process in order to test each algorithm\u2019s ability to classify new songs to their correct genre, and we analyze the results yielded by which algorithm to understand which algorithm works best in principle given this particular data set.","topics":[],"score":214073,"global_rank":253815},{"name":"Chrysippean/Singular-Value-Decomposition-Eigenfaces","owner":"Chrysippean","html_url":"https://github.com/Chrysippean/Singular-Value-Decomposition-Eigenfaces","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"MATLAB","description":"We use the singular value decomposition on a matrix of pictures and explore the picture details captured by the modes produced in the matrix decomposition. We also compare the significance of each mode, and how details vary as we increase the number of modes active in image reconstruction. ","topics":[],"score":214073,"global_rank":253816},{"name":"qzysw123456/MultiLayerPerceptron","owner":"qzysw123456","html_url":"https://github.com/qzysw123456/MultiLayerPerceptron","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Matlab","description":null,"topics":[],"score":214073,"global_rank":253818},{"name":"qzysw123456/SVM","owner":"qzysw123456","html_url":"https://github.com/qzysw123456/SVM","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Matlab","description":null,"topics":[],"score":214073,"global_rank":253819}]